  "problem": "The matrix\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}a & -\\sqrt{3}-6 \\\\ b & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nrepresents the linear transformation that acts on a vector in ${R}^{2}$ as follows (in the order given):\n\n- It rotates the vector by $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ radians **clockwise** about the origin, then\n\n- applies a shear transformation to the result with a shear factor of $6$ parallel to the $x$-axis, and finally\n\n- reflects the result about the $y$-axis.\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b?$",
